2 & I=\int_{-\pi / 2}^{\pi / 2} \sin ^2 x d x=\frac{1}{2} \int_{-\pi / 2}^{\pi / 2}(1-\cos 2 x) d x \\
\Rightarrow \quad \mathrm{I} & =\frac{1}{4}\left[x+\frac{\sin 2 x}{2}\right]_{-\pi / 2}^{\pi / 2} \\
